### Adapted from RNS

All entries were read from RNS 1.5.7 (PyPI wheel `rns-1.5.7-py3-none-any.whl`,
SHA-256 0e4aaf8cc47f770da34572d2215b45fea900e104b009551600eb9741a41faddf), host
side only: RNode firmware is not read. The behaviour was adopted and the Rust
is written for this crate; no Python was translated line by line. The findings
are recorded in `design_docs/2026-10-09_rns_157_interface_review.md`.

From the interface batch (2026-10-09):

- The RNode host follows RNS's configuration semantics: airtime locks (percent
  x 100) sent after the coding rate and before the radio state; echoes of
  frequency (within 100 Hz), bandwidth, TX power and spreading factor checked
  before going online, airtime-lock echoes recorded but never compared; a
  firmware floor of 1.52; parameter ranges. Stricter than RNS: the coding rate
  and a missing frequency echo are checked, and a low firmware is a fault
  rather than a process exit. RNS `Interfaces/RNodeInterface.py` 40-120,
  151-160, 307-349, 428-500, 619-695, 896-925.
  Targets: `src/rnode.rs`, `src/rnode/config.rs`.
- Device errors 0x05 and 0x06 are recorded and others are fatal; a reset while
  online is fatal on every platform (RNS checks it on ESP32 only); detach sends
  RADIO_STATE 0 then LEAVE; a partial frame is dropped after 100 ms idle; a
  failed port is reopened after 5 s; READY flow control, with a 5 s unlock RNS
  lacks. RNS `Interfaces/RNodeInterface.py` 711-744, 1076-1209.
  Targets: `src/rnode.rs`, `src/serial/`.
- The hardware MTU is 508, so a full packet with an 8-byte access code crosses.
  RNS `Interfaces/RNodeInterface.py` 110, 195, 770.
  Targets: `src/rnode/config.rs`, `src/radio_io.rs`.
